+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ per cell for the lookup table (33 entries) [S1, unofficial]. No global data structures are required [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Measured Performance:** Implemented in the HIGZ graphics package [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Guarantees topological correctness for the trilinear interpolant. Resolves holes that appear in standard Marching Cubes when adjacent cells have complementary ambiguous configurations (e.g., Config 6 sharing a face with Complement of Config 3) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** The lookup table is larger (33 vs 15). Some cases require an additional internal vertex, which can complicate mesh post-processing (e.g., smoothing) as it introduces a vertex not on the grid edges [S1, unofficial].
